<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco posts 8 pct rise '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco posts 8 pct rise '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings for 1996 for Swedish engineering group Atlas Copco AB.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 3,070  vs  2,840</p>
<p> Sales				     25,121  vs 24,454</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)	     10.56  vs   9.93</p>
<p> Order bookings			  25,159  vs 24,843</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (SKR)		 3.75   vs  3.00</p>
<p> Operating costs			 21,419  vs 21,077</p>
<p> Depreciation				 771  vs    712</p>
<p> Profit after depreciation	    2,931  vs  2,665</p>
<p> Net interest				 127  vs    129</p>
<p> Dividend payment			    14  vs	2</p>
<p> Currency exchange difference    CHARGE 2  vs     45 CHARGE</p>
<p> Associate interests			  0  vs     89</p>
<p> Tax					  1,107  vs    990</p>
<p> Minorities				    25  vs     27</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,938  vs  1,823</p>
<p>NOTE - In a Reuters poll of 14 analysts, expectations averaged a profit after financial items of 3.03 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
